# CODEOWNERS
#
# Maps paths to the people or teams who must review changes to them. Syntax:
# a path pattern (gitignore-style), then one or more @username / @org/team
# handles. Later matching lines override earlier ones, so put broad defaults
# first and narrower overrides below them.
#
# Example (uncomment and edit for your org):
# * @your-org/maintainers
#
# More examples of the shape once you have real owners:
# /docs/          @your-org/docs-team
# /ops/           @your-org/platform-team
# *.sql           @your-org/db-reviewers
#
# This file only binds when branch protection requires review from code
# owners on the paths it covers — ops/bootstrap-repo.sh configures that
# requirement. An empty or absent CODEOWNERS with that setting on means no
# path has an enforced owner yet; add rows as ownership becomes real.
